From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 27 Mar 2024 10:47:48 +0100
Subject: refactor: expose file system access blocklist

This CL exposes the file system access blocklist publicly so that we can leverage
it in Electron and prevent drift from Chrome's blocklist. We should look for a way
to upstream this change to Chrome.

NormalizeFilePathForBlocklist() and GenerateBlockPaths() are declared as static
members in the header, and their definitions (along with the NormalizeFilePath()
and MaybeStripMacDataVolumePrefix() helpers they use) are moved verbatim out of
chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.cc into a new
chrome_file_system_access_blocklist.cc, which Electron compiles. Upstream changes
to the blocklist therefore conflict on the hunk that removes them from
chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.cc instead of being silently
dropped; when resolving such a conflict, carry the change over into
chrome_file_system_access_blocklist.cc.

